# Blue Ward gives Bot2's Savannah Lions protection from blue (CR 702.16). On turn 3 Bot1 cannot target the Lions with
# Curious Obsession, a blue Aura spell (CR 702.16b; the refusal, and the runner offers it again with mana to spare),
# and Fugitive Wizard attacking into it is blocked by the Lions: the Wizard's damage is blue and prevented
# (CR 702.16e), so the 2/1 Lions survives with no damage marked (without Blue Ward it would die) while the Wizard dies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Fugitive Wizard
Curious Obsession
Island
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Savannah Lions
Blue Ward
Plains x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fugitive Wizard.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Savannah Lions.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Blue Ward.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Curious Obsession.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions)
Bot1.Attack(Fugitive Wizard > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Savannah Lions > Fugitive Wizard)
[T3 Bot1.CombatDamage]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions.Damage = 0
[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions.ProtectionFrom = Blue
Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions.Damage = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Blue Ward.AttachedTo = Savannah Lions
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Fugitive Wizard
